## 1. Scope

This audit covers plugin catalog, versions, manifest normalization, signatures, install policy, review, lifecycle, supply-chain scanning, runtime policy linkage, UI behavior, and AgentMesh/SDK marketplace surfaces. It inspects `product_platform/marketplace`, marketplace migrations, marketplace UI, `agent-marketplace`, AgentMesh fallback marketplace, and plugin-related runtime kill switch code. Relevant benchmarks are JFrog MCP Registry/AI Catalog, OpenAI tool approval patterns, Arcade/Composio tool governance, and enterprise software supply-chain controls. Out of scope: MCP proxy runtime behavior, covered in MCP.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

Product Platform has marketplace catalog migrations, including plugin versions and installs in `0023_marketplace_catalog.up.sql`, policy results in `0024_marketplace_policy_results.up.sql`, and installations in `0025_marketplace_installations.up.sql`. Models, policy, quality scoring, signing, and repository logic live under `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/marketplace`. The frontend marketplace page lives in `frontend/src/features/marketplace/MarketplacePage.tsx`. The Python SDK repo includes `packages/agent-marketplace` with Ed25519 signing helpers and `packages/agentmesh` fallback marketplace code. Runtime kill-switch models mention plugin targets.

Current workflow: plugins can be imported, reviewed, checked by policy, signed in a demo manner in Product Platform, installed, and shown in UI. Install policy is permissive by default, package provenance is not verified, and runtime enforcement is not generated from approved plugin manifests.

